&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper Security is hiring an IT Support Specialist to join our EMEA IT team and provide hands-on technical support to employees across our Cork office and wider European organization. Qualified candidates must permanently reside in Ireland. This is a hybrid position based within a commutable distance to our Cork, Ireland office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper’s cybersecurity software is trusted by millions of people and thousands of organisations globally. Keeper is published in 23 languages and sold in over 150 countries. Join one of the fastest-growing cybersecurity companies and help deliver reliable, secure and responsive IT support for Keeper employees across EMEA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Keeper&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper Security is one of the fastest-growing cybersecurity software companies that protects thousands of organisations and millions of people in over 150 countries. Keeper is a pioneer of zero-knowledge and zero-trust security built for any IT environment. Its core offering, KeeperPAM®, is an AI-enabled, cloud-native platform that protects all users, devices and infrastructure from cyber attacks. Recognised for its innovation in the Gartner Magic Quadrant for Privileged Access Management (PAM), Keeper secures passwords and passkeys, infrastructure secrets, remote connections and endpoints with role-based enforcement policies, least privilege and just-in-time access. Learn why Keeper is trusted by leading organisations to defend against modern adversaries at &lt;a href=&quot;http://keepersecurity.com&quot;&gt;KeeperSecurity.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an IT Support Specialist, you will provide Level 1 and Level 2 technical support to Keeper employees, helping resolve hardware, software, account access and workplace technology issues. You will be a key point of contact for employees in the Cork office while also supporting remote users across EMEA. This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys troubleshooting, working directly with users and keeping workplace technology running smoothly. You will support employee onboarding and offboarding, device provisioning, account administration, asset management and day-to-day IT operations while escalating more complex infrastructure or security issues when appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Level 1 and Level 2 technical support for employees across Windows and macOS environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot laptops, peripherals, operating systems, business applications and user access issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provision, configure and deploy laptops and other equipment for new employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support employee onboarding and offboarding, including account setup, access changes and equipment management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer user accounts and access across Google Workspace, Microsoft, SaaS applications and other enterprise systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and track IT hardware, software assets and inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose connectivity, VPN, Wi-Fi and basic network issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support conference rooms, audiovisual equipment and other workplace technology within the Cork office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document incidents, resolutions and troubleshooting steps within the IT ticketing system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex issues to senior IT, Security or Infrastructure teams with clear technical documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with endpoint management, software deployment, patching and device security controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow IT security, access control and data protection policies when supporting users and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain internal IT documentation, knowledge articles and standard operating procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted tools such as Claude, ChatGPT or similar platforms to support troubleshooting, documentation, research and workflow efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in IT support, service desk, desktop support or a related technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience supporting Windows and macOS users in a business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting hardware, software, account access and common workplace technology issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Google Workspace, Microsoft technologies or similar enterprise productivity platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience provisioning and supporting employee laptops and peripherals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity and access management concepts, including user accounts, groups and permissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of networking concepts including TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, Wi-Fi and VPNs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with ticketing systems and documenting technical issues and resolutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and customer service skills when working with technical and non-technical users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple support requests and prioritise issues based on urgency and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to use AI-assisted tools effectively to improve troubleshooting, research and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified candidates must permanently reside in Ireland and be able to commute to Keeper’s Cork office as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting SaaS or cybersecurity organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile device management or endpoint management platforms&lt;

&lt;p&gt;Serving as the EMEA anchor for MongoDB&#39;s Global Enterprise Technology (GET) team, this position acts as a primary technical DRI for enterprise user support, office technology, and regional incident escalation in the GMT/IST time zone. You hold end-to-end operational responsibility for delivering high-touch, reliable IT services—from onboarding hardware provisioning and daily ticket triage to AV room management and high-visibility regional event support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role prioritizes proactive support over passive ticketing. By monitoring system health, verifying endpoint configurations, and identifying friction points early, you ensure business continuity for teams across the EMEA region. You combine strong technical diagnostics across macOS, Windows, identity, and SaaS tooling with hands-on AV expertise for Dublin meeting spaces, acting as a trusted partner to local leaders and cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The operational foundation of GET relies on intelligent automation, structured workflows, and data-informed decision-making. Routine health checks, diagnostics, and repetitive provisioning tasks are streamlined through intelligent tooling, freeing your focus for complex technical problem-solving, live event execution, and relationship building. In this environment, you are encouraged to leverage emerging AI productivity tools and automation scripts to continuously optimize service delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role requires technical versatility, disciplined execution in shared team queues, discreet handling of sensitive data, and clear communication across a globally distributed IT organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Dublin for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Enterprise Support &amp;amp; Technical Ownership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Queue Ownership: Ownership of the regional end-user support queue. Deliver rapid, high-quality resolution for macOS, Windows, identity, mobile, and SaaS software issues across the EMEA region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship Management: Partner closely with regional department heads, office administrators, and local stakeholders to maintain strong alignment between IT services and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive Resolution: Monitor endpoint health and system alerts to remediate device, network, or security issues before they impact productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SLA &amp;amp; Workflow Tracking: Keep structured ticket workflows updated with clear diagnostic notes, tracking work against key SLAs (MTTR, FTTR, and CSAT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Lifecycle Management &amp;amp; Onboarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware Provisioning: Manage procurement, device configuration, endpoint deployment, and asset tracking for laptops, mobile devices, and peripherals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboarding Execution: Ensure new hires receive fully configured hardware and role-based application entitlements prior to their start date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offboarding &amp;amp; Asset Recovery: Execute secure, compliant offboarding workflows, ensuring timely hardware collection, account deprovisioning, and data destruction standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidentiality &amp;amp; Data Governance: Handle all employee data, sensitive operational context, and security entitlements in strict compliance with company confidentiality standards and NDA requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Global Handoffs &amp;amp; Incident Response&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow-the-Sun Operational Coverage: Participate in the global 24/7 handoff standard—APAC → EMEA → AMERICAS—passing overnight incidents, open risks, and active escalation threads at shift boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalation Coordination: Hand specialized infrastructure or security elements to L3/Engineering teams while retaining ownership of user-impacting regional threads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-Call Rotation: Participate in the regional after-hours or weekend incident rotation, applying quick diagnostic workarounds and escalating according to severity matrices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4. AV Systems, Office Infrastructure &amp;amp; Events&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conference Room Maintenance: Maintain operational readiness for Dublin office Zoom Rooms, Teams rooms, microphones, displays, and control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event Support: Lead technical preparation and live support for EMEA All Hands, town halls, quarterly business reviews, and regional leadership meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network &amp;amp; Workplace Collaboration: Partner with Network/AV Engineering and Facilities teams to resolve physical office connectivity issues, room remediation, and hardware upgrades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5. Process Discipline &amp;amp; AI-Driven Efficiency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured Ticket Hygiene: Maintain accurate ticket estimates, DRI tags, and clear definitions of done in Jira or similar enterprise service desk tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Toil Reduction: Utilize AI agent-assist tools, virtual assistants, and workflow scripting (Python, PowerShell, or API integrations) to eliminate manual tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge Management: Author and update internal technical runbooks and end-user self-service documentation in Confluence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success Measures &amp;amp; Expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, success is measured by concrete operational outcomes and your ability to scale regional IT support alongside enterprise growth:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service Excellence &amp;amp; SLA Rigor: Maintain a consistent track record of hitting target SLAs (≥95%) across regional queues with flat-to-up CSAT scores, shifting the operational ratio decisively from reactive ticket firefighting to proactive, automated issue re

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper Security is seeking a dynamic and motivated Marketing Intern to support the EMEA Growth Marketing team. This internship offers a unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience in B2B marketing, demand generation, and marketing operations within the cybersecurity industry. They will play an active role in supporting marketing campaigns, lead generation initiatives, and digital marketing activities across the EMEA region. This is a 100% remote internship from select locations, with an opportunity to work a hybrid schedule for those candidates based in the Cork City area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper’s cybersecurity software is trusted by millions of people and thousands of organisations, globally. Keeper is published in 23 languages and is sold in over 150 countries. Join one of the fastest-growing cybersecurity companies and gain valuable skills assisting our marketing department in our promotional efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Keeper&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper Security is a leading cybersecurity software company that protects thousands of organizations and millions of people in more than 150 countries. Keeper delivers a powerful zero-trust and zero-knowledge solution built to meet the stringent requirements of public sector IT environments. Its flagship offering, KeeperPAM®, is an AI-enabled, cloud-native platform that protects users, devices and critical infrastructure from cyber attacks. Recognized in the Gartner® Magic QuadrantTM for Privileged Access Management (PAM), Keeper combines robust compliance with unmatched visibility and control. With industry-leading certifications, Keeper provides the security assurance public sector organizations require. Learn why agencies trust Keeper to defend against today’s sophisticated adversaries at &lt;a href=&quot;http://keepersecurity.com&quot;&gt;KeeperSecurity.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Intern will report to the Senior Marketing Manager, EMEA and will be responsible for supporting the EMEA Growth Marketing team on daily tasks and projects. This is a 3-month internship with the possibility of extension, contingent on company needs and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a paid internship designed to offer professional experience in marketing and demand generation. &lt;strong&gt;Please note that we do not offer school credit for this internship.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the EMEA team execute and manage marketing/demand generation activities, including field events, email campaigns, display ads, webinars, social media initiatives and content development that drive new business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with setting up digital marketing campaigns in LinkedIn, XING, Reddit, Demandbase, HubSpot.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide general marketing support to the team for the coordination of campaigns and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other Keeper marketing teams to implement international programs like PPC, SEO, PR and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with monitoring campaign performance and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current enrollment in or recent completion of a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree (Undergraduate or Postgraduate degree) in Marketing, Communications, Business or a related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with a commitment to accuracy and quality in all deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment and take initiative on assigned tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic working knowledge of Google (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive) and Microsoft Office products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing automation platforms and CRM systems would be a distinct advantage (e.g. HubSpot, Marketo, Pardot, Salesforce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous marketing internship or relevant work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeper Security, Inc. is an equal opportunity employer and participant, we celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf0&quot;&gt;Keeper Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt;This notice explains how Keeper Security processes your personal data during recruitment. Depending on the role and location, the Controller of personal data (the organization responsible for determining why and how personal data is processed) will be Keeper Security Inc. (US), Keeper Security EMEA Ltd. (Ireland), or Keeper Security APAC K.K (Japan).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt; 1. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf0&quot;&gt;Data We Collect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;pf0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt;Information You provide:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;pf1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt;Contact details, CV/resume, cover letter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;pf1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt;Employment history, qualifications, work eligibility&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;pf1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cf1&quot;&gt;Application responses and uploade

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tines is the intelligent workflow company that powers some of the world&#39;s most important workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tines has been supporting IT and security teams from a diverse range of customers, including Canva, Reddit, SAP, Coinbase, Mars, Fin (Intercom), and McKesson.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tines 3B, launched in 2026, is the next generation of Tines – a single, secure environment for every team’s apps, agents and automations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an integrator across the entire tech stack, Tines is vendor-agnostic integrating with any API-enabled service. This flexibility enables our customers to achieve their highest-priority goals faster. Tines has security woven into its DNA, and our platform is secure and private by design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tines, we&#39;re driven by our values of Simplicity, Speed, and Soundness. We&#39;re committed to delivering exceptional customer experiences while fostering a company culture that nurtures individual curiosity, growth, and integrity. We’re excited about what’s next, and we’re looking for others to join us on our journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A technical support engineer provides technical support and consultation to customers and colleagues. They are essential in troubleshooting and diagnosing technical issues, providing timely resolutions, and ensuring customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position focuses on responding to, owning, and resolving users&#39; technical queries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule:&lt;/strong&gt; This role works &lt;strong&gt;Wednesday-Saturday&amp;nbsp;6:00 am – 16:00 pm local time&lt;/strong&gt;, with weekday shifts embedded alongside the wider Support team and weekend shifts (Saturday) worked solo and unsupervised, handing over to and from other regional shifts as part of a follow-the-sun rotation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling technical inquiries received across multiple channels (Slack, in-app chat, and email), maintaining high standards for responsiveness and ticket hygiene&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot customer inquiries, including but not limited to API integrations, systems issues, network and security-related impediments, 3rd party integrations, and multi-product workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpreting API documents and creating Tines workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configuring and implementing authentication types like OAuth and JWT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documenting the steps needed to connect to new tools or document any new workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, troubleshooting, documenting, and modifying workflows on remote sessions with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships with other team members within Support and the wider company, acting as the voice of the customer, and maintaining continuity with the team&#39;s priorities and open issues despite working outside standard team hours for part of the week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Customer Support resources and deliver meaningful product feedback as the voice of the customer to leadership and relevant internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify improvements to the product, identify bugs, and otherwise determine high-impact opportunities to enhance the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing clear, structured handover notes at the start and end of each shift so incoming and outgoing regional teams have full context with no gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making independent judgment calls on prioritization, troubleshooting approach, and escalation while working solo during unsupervised weekend hours, including recognizing when an issue requires paging an on-call engineer or escalating outside normal hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will bring to the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of technical support experience within a SaaS environment, ideally in automation or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience constructing, testing, and debugging REST and GraphQL API requests, using developer documentation and SDK examples to understand and troubleshoot integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to implementing or troubleshooting AI actions and agentic workflows, including LLM APIs, prompt structures, and protocols such as MCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting in a web-based environment, including HTTP, SSL, and basic networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, analytical, and troubleshooting skills, including clear written communication for handover documentation, given the reliance on asynchronous handoffs with other regional shifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex technical concepts to non-technical and technical stakeholders alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling inbound technical customer requests in various form channels (chat, email)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of customer empathy, urgency, and technical competency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, goal-oriented, with excellent organizational and time management skills, and a consistent quality bar, whether working alongside the team or solo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with at least one modern programming language, such as Python, TypeScript, or Ruby&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with query languages such as SQL and GraphQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work autonomously, make sound decisions without direct supervision, and exercise good judgment on when to escalate versus solve independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and self-directed problem-solving, including researching solutions independently using documentation, runbooks, and prior tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience and composure when handling difficult technical or customer issues without immediate backup or a second opinion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to context-sw

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a recent graduate with a passion for sales and technology, eager to kickstart your career in a dynamic SaaS environment? At New Relic, we&#39;re seeking an Associate Sales Development Representative to join our team and be at the forefront of our go-to-market strategy. This role is perfect for ambitious individuals looking to develop their sales skills while working in an environment that values innovation, personal growth, and professional excellence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join New Relic?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we offer a transformative experience to kickstart your career in sales and in the cutting-edge world of observability. Our Sales team is at the forefront of our go-to-market strategy, partnering closely with Account Executives (AEs) to deliver impactful business outcomes for our customers. You’ll join a collaborative, high-energy team with personalized coaching, world-class tools, and significant opportunities for career growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we believe in supporting our team with the resources, mentorship, and opportunities to build a lasting career in sales. You’ll be part of a culture where hard work is rewarded, teamwork drives success, and every win is celebrated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in building something great. Apply now!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an SDR, you will be the first point of contact for prospects and customers reaching out to New Relic about their digital transformation journey. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inbound leads from email, phone, and Live Sales Chat within your assigned region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify prospective customers interested in New Relic solutions as part of their digital transformation journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze customer needs in terms of current business obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with account managers to progress business-ready opportunities and ensure a smooth handover for the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create qualified business leads to achieve a quarterly quota, consistently meeting or exceeding targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master social selling and communication skills, actively using various tools including social media and web-based tools to engage with customers and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve a high level of collaboration within the Sales Development team and with key stakeholders in Sales and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Degree&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in technology with a customer-first mindset and enthusiasm for understanding technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grit, drive, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, goal-oriented environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for sales, with aspirations to grow into a closing role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive and agile mindset, enthusiastic and genuinely passionate about this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills (written and verbal) with the ability to engage prospects at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience and a positive attitude when facing challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills with a sharp focus on goals and a clear approach for achieving them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with cold calling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid position. Three days per week in our Dublin office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a customer-facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient attitude and determination to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to objections and turn “no” into “let’s talk further.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to working with teams and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native proficiency in second European language (German, French, Dutch, Spanish, Italian, Polish)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cold calling experience: previous experience in a role that required outbound cold calling and willingness and comfort in making outbound calls daily as a primary function of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
