&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Platform Sales team works with B2B software platforms to help them facilitate payments for their customers using Stripe Connect. Our users are software businesses who serve other businesses — platforms like Shopify, Treatwell, Sage, and DesignMyNight already rely on Stripe to power their payments infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of the Platforms team, you will manage and deepen relationships with a named account list while identifying new growth opportunities and finding ways Stripe can exceed expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive (Grower), you will build partnerships between Stripe and the most innovative and fastest-growing software platforms in the world, helping them understand how Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure can make payments a true competitive advantage for their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and develop a named account list, building account plans to win and expand business with upper middle market and enterprise SaaS platform companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain key relationships with C-level executives, orchestrating the right executive touchpoints throughout the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for upper middle market and enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with stakeholders across Engineering, Product, and Finance to lead complex product workshops and financial analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft and lead complex, bespoke commercial and contractual negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping our platform partnership strategy and building repeatable processes and scaled engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to help shape product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson and relationship manager, comfortable engaging in both business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of an organisation — including the CEO, CFO, CTO . You have experience with upper middle market and enterprise companies, a deep understanding of the buyer journey, and the ability to lead complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding combined with technical knowledge. You&#39;re naturally analytical and enjoy exploring business models and helping users quantify their investment decisions. You&#39;re energised by prospecting and capable of independently leading a full sales cycle from start to finish — and you like to build, actively contributing to sales process development, value proposition articulation, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of sales experience selling a technical product or service, preferably at an API-first company, with a consistent track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading complex, multi-party sales from inception to close in a highly consultative manner, including developing strategies and building compelling value propositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong listening skills and the ability to quickly become a trusted resource for decision-makers across technology and finance organisations within software companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical problems and position Stripe&#39;s solutions to address them effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the software landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and Nordic Languages (Swedish, Danish, Finnish,Norwegian)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments or financial technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a sales or customer-facing role at a high-growth technology company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Sales is a team of deep functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Stripe is investing in building out its Fraud &amp;amp; Risk Product Sales team and as an Account Executive you will be a critical part of the team driving the growth of this product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, Product focusing on Fraud &amp;amp; Risk products, you will use your sales and product expertise to help drive product market fit &amp;amp; growth of Stripe’s fraud fighting products and solutions. You will collaborate with product, engineering and marketing teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You will be instrumental in leading in depth product discussions with existing and prospect users globally – and building and executing against our go to market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including CEOs, CTOs, and Chief Risk Officers. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding. You’re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives). You’re excited to become an expert and to share your knowledge. You’re an organized self-starter, an excellent communicator who is highly analytical and has a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new business and revenue growth by selling Radar, Managed Risk, Dispute Resolution, and more, to a variety of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex new and expansion deals related to Stripe’s Fraud &amp;amp; Risk product offerings, capabilities, and tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the sales process and what competitors offer in terms of fraud fighting capabilities, with a strong emphasis to overcoming competition to win all deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and relay customer feedback and findings to inform Stripe’s product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing and Account teams to help amplify our growth trajectory globally&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 - 10+ years of customer facing experience at a leading technology or payments company and a track record of top performance, working specifically on enterprise or strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Display a deep passion for fraud prevention and develop deep expertise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building trusted advisor relationships with senior business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter capable of operating independently to drive meaningful business results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience specifically selling fraud solutions for payments to enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
