&lt;p&gt;At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dedication to &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;remote-first work&lt;/a&gt;, and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Senior International Payroll Analyst.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payroll team is seeking an experienced, self-motivated, and systems-savvy Senior Payroll Analyst, EMEA Payroll to lead payroll operations across the EMEA region. This role will be responsible for ensuring accurate, timely, and compliant payroll delivery across multiple countries, while assisting the EMEA regional payroll team, managing external vendor relationships, strengthening controls, and driving process standardization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sr Payroll Analyst, International Payroll will partner closely with People, Benefits, Equity, Finance, Accounting, HRIS, Legal, and external payroll providers to support a high-quality employee experience and scalable payroll operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the payroll processing and management of assigned payrolls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ad hoc projects related to payroll and benefits for our international entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After necessary training, support the international payroll processing for multiple countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive the local international payroll news related to potential housing allowance, income tax withholding calculations, miscellaneous payroll inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively collaborate with the payroll vendor to ensure that all pay impacting transactions are collected, processed and reported timely and accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Accounting Team with payroll journal and accrual preparations and the reconciliations of payroll general ledger balances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain relationships with key stakeholders and provide support and input when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and improve payroll processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver excellent Employee experience in relation to payroll onboarding, ad-hoc queries and annual tax reporting process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to all legal and internal deadlines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand employment tax requirements relating to compensation and benefits, including equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the tax reviewer/payroll auditor requests and payroll inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve parafiscales and social benefits inquires from local jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the annual income tax filing process where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve payroll-related documentation and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience managing payroll processing internationally with working experience in accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with processing equity transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance or another relevant field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discipline and ability to meet tight deadlines, and prioritize competing workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, and verbal communication skills in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very strong analytical and problem-solving skills while keeping customer experience top of mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Workday and with outside payroll providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer service focus with the ability and sound judgment to handle highly sensitive information.&lt;/li&

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fin.ai/&quot;&gt;Fin&lt;/a&gt;, now part of Salesforce, is on a mission to help businesses provide perfect customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI Agent Fin is the highest-performing AI Customer Agent on the market today, enabling businesses to deliver impeccable, always-on customer support across the customer journey, from service, to sales, to ecommerce. Powered by our own AI models, Fin resolves complex customer issues end-to-end across every channel, with minimal set-up and integration. Fin can also be combined with our natively integrated Intercom help desk, giving modern support teams one single system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with Salesforce, the #1 AI CRM, where humans with agents drive customer success, we&#39;re building the future of customer experience. Here, ambition meets action. Tech meets trust. And innovation isn&#39;t a buzzword, it&#39;s a way of life. The world of work as we know it is changing, and we&#39;re looking for Trailblazers who are passionate about bettering business and the world through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to level up your career at the company leading workforce transformation in the agentic era? You&#39;re in the right place. Agentforce is the future of AI, and you are the future of Salesforce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s the opportunity?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a proven operator to redesign how Customer Support works across Human and AI Support. Fin is an AI-first support organisation, and our processes should reflect that: you’ll have a genuine licence to rethink, rebuild or retire existing processes from first principles, not just refine them. This is a hands-on and strategic role: you keep day-to-day operations running well and fix what is broken, while building a long-term process strategy for the whole of Customer Support. You will also help embed Continuous Improvement, using conversation and quality insights to decide what we fix, retrain and prioritise next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support at Fin changes constantly, and our processes need to keep pace with this level of change. The right candidate is exceptionally customer-focused, comes from a customer-facing background, and has experience leading and managing processes and workflows in a large organisation. You bring clear opinions and recommendations, work with a high degree of autonomy, and hold the line on the customer experience when working with other teams. You combine exceptional project management and attention to detail with a data-driven mindset and a proven ability to influence and collaborate at every level of the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What will I be doing?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge and, where warranted, completely redesign existing processes and ways of working: you won’t be constrained by ‘how we’ve always done it’, and you’ll have the support of Customer Support leadership to make bold changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the framework for reviewing, prioritising and implementing Customer Support processes and workflows across Human and AI Support, so every change improves the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a long-term process strategy and roadmap for Support, balancing quick wins and immediate fixes with strategic improvements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the long-term Continuous Improvement strategy for Support, setting priorities and a roadmap that cover both Human and AI support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clear proposals and recommendations to leadership, and act on them with autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams outside of Customer Support to design processes that work end to end, agreeing clear ownership, handoffs and shared goals so the customer experience holds across team boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process design and improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse current processes across Human and AI Support and decide whether each should be improved, redesigned from scratch or removed entirely. Where AI and automation can fundamentally change how the work gets done, lead that transformation rather than layering them onto legacy workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day operational process fixes and keep existing processes effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and roll out new or improved processes, solo or with SMEs, partnering closely with Customer Support leaders and ICs in every region so processes work globally, not just for one region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement process control metrics, and monitor process performance and KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to find where processes are failing, size the opportunity and prove the impact of changes, building and maintaining dashboards and reports that give leaders a clear view of process health across Human and AI support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with internal policies and external regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and iterate on the Continuous Improvement framework, using insights from both Human and AI support to drive improvements, across Enablement, Quality, AI support, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn insights into a prioritised improvement backlog, with clear owners across respective internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track whether each improvement worked, using before-and-after measures such as repeat contact rate, resolution rate and CX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn customer conversation data into clear, actionable insights for Product, Engineering and other teams, giving them evidence to shape priorities and roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholders and delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&

