&lt;p&gt;The Vice President of EMEA Marketing will lead MongoDB’s regional marketing strategy, driving pipeline and revenue growth across one of the company’s most strategic markets. This executive will translate global priorities into focused regional investments, build strong partnerships with Sales and GTM leadership, and deliver measurable business impact across customer acquisition and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond delivering near-term results, this leader will help transform how regional marketing operates. Partnering with the Global SVP of Revenue Marketing, they will leverage AI, shared capabilities, and new operating models to simplify execution, increase productivity, and drive greater impact without proportional increases in cost or headcount.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible leadership opportunity for a commercially minded, AI-forward marketing executive who can operate at scale, develop exceptional teams, and shape the future of regional marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role reports to the Global SVP of Revenue Marketing. Candidates should be based in London or Dublin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set regional strategy and lead execution: Own EMEA marketing strategy and business outcomes; Translate global growth priorities into a regional go-to-market strategy, with clear accountability for marketing’s contribution to pipeline, revenue, customer acquisition, and expansion.;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate pipeline and revenue growth: Partner with EMEA Sales and global GTM leaders to align marketing investment with business priorities, improve account engagement, and deliver measurable commercial outcomes across enterprise and developer-led motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build sales and partner alignment: Establish strong operating rhythms with regional Sales and partner teams to align on business priorities, pipeline goals, and account strategy; Leverage their market and customer insights to shape regional marketing investments, strengthen account engagement, and drive coordinated execution that supports pipeline and revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transform the regional operating model: Partner with the Global SVP of Revenue Marketing to redesign how regional marketing operates Leverage AI, automation, and shared capabilities to simplify workflows, increase productivity, and improve business impact without proportional increases in cost or headcount; Test new ways of working that combine clear business ownership, shared AI capabilities, and specialized expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Marketing: Work as a trusted peer with the global Marketing leadership team, including Revenue, Product, Corporate, and Comms, to align on shared priorities, balance global consistency with regional needs, and model a collaborative, one-team approach across the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize and deliver high-impact regional programs: Make deliberate investment choices across enterprise demand generation, account-based engagement, developer programs, partners, and events; Focus resources on the markets, accounts, and activities most likely to drive pipeline and revenue, using shared capabilities to scale execution efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring market insight into decision-making: Track customer needs, market dynamics, competitive activity, and addressable opportunity across EMEA; Use these insights to inform regional investment, positioning, and go-to-market choices, strengthen MongoDB’s competitive position, and establish it as the data platform in the AI era&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a high-performing team: Lead, coach, and grow a diverse regional marketing organization; Set clear expectations, develop future leaders, and foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, and continuous learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively at scale: Work across regional Marketing, Product Marketing, Corporate Marketing, Developer Relations, Communications, and other teams to create cohesive customer experiences and continuously improve regional processes, measurement, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We’re Excited About You Because&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience: You bring 15+ years of experience in demand generation, field, or revenue marketing, including leadership roles across EMEA in enterprise technology; Experience in cloud, database, AI, or enterprise software is especially relevant; You have operated in complex, strategic sales environments and understand how marketing programs and technology contribute to customer and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled leadership: Experience leading regional marketing in a complex, multinational enterprise technology organization, with demonstrated ability to operate at scale and manage significant marketing investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth and pipeline impact: You have a track record of developing and executing regional marketing strategies that contribute to pipeline, revenue growth, customer acquisition, expansion, and market leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern marketing expertise: You bring strong expertise in ABM, integrated demand generation, and the enterprise marketing technology ecosystem, with the judgment to select approaches that fit the business and market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer and enterprise buying dynamics: You understand how product-led growth, developer adoption, technical evaluation, and executive decision-making intersect in enterprise technology purchases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-forward operating leadership: You have demonstrated the ability to use AI and automation to redesign marketing workflows, improve productivity, and increase business impact; You understand how to lead organizational change, develop new capabilities, and rethink roles and processes rather than simply introducing new tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional influence: You build trust

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager, Mid-Market Sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager, Mid-Market Sales, you will provide strategy, mentorship, and guidance for a team of Mid-Market Account Executives. This role impacts one of the largest lines of business in the company, ultimately bringing a proven product to a multi-billion dollar market and selling into companies from 1,000 to 5,000 employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivate your team to exceed objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain accurate team forecasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, oversee, and train a team of Mid-Market Account Executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive lead generation, high activity standards, and pipeline management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate the ramp up for all new team members, coaching them to success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the sales funnel from prospect to close and create metrics to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in tech industry direct sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong preference for Italian (and/or Spanish) language fluency alongside core relevant regional sales experience in Italy and Iberia among others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with SaaS/Cloud and Salesforce&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to accurately forecast team performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about coaching, mentorship, and team management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by helping people grow with a desire to continue learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who thrives in a high-growth, rapidly changing marketplace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven in overseeing an outbound sales team in all areas of the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your experience, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High income earning opportunities based on performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity for Presidents Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire stock equity (RSU) and employee stock purchase plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous professional development, product training, and career pathing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales training in MEDDIC and Command of the Message&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intra-departmental mentor and buddy program for in-house networking&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive company culture, opportunity to join our Community Guilds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous global benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
